{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1369,
    "dDurationMs": 5311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airplanes stay in the air because of one simple\nfact: there is no net force on them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6680,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And with no net force, an object at rest stays\nat rest, and an object in motion stays that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11509,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way – even if it’s in midair 10 km above\nthe earth’s surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15309,
    "dDurationMs": 3831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now of course it’s not like there aren’t\nforces acting on the airplane; gravity pulls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19140,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down on the plane itself plus all of the people\nand baggage inside, and every single air molecule"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23340,
    "dDurationMs": 4009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is shot through the engine or collides\nwith the fuselage or wings pushes on the plane"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27349,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28349,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if all of these forces are balanced – in\nparticular, if the air molecules push the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31939,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plane UP enough to counteract gravity – then\nthe plane stays up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35829,
    "dDurationMs": 4361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Getting air molecules to push the plane up\nis the crucial part of flying, and planes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40190,
    "dDurationMs": 4869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do this by making sure the undersides of the\nwings crash into more air molecules more violently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45059,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the upper sides of the wings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46559,
    "dDurationMs": 4011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a plane is parked on the ground, air\nmolecules bounce off of the top and bottom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50570,
    "dDurationMs": 3519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the wings in roughly equal amounts, or\nwith “equal pressure.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54089,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No lift."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55089,
    "dDurationMs": 4581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in motion, the curved shape of the wings\nand their slightly inclined angle means that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59670,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bottoms smash into more air molecules\nthan before (and smash harder into those molecules),"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64680,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the pressure on the bottom of the wing\ngoes up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67180,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In addition, fewer air molecules now strike\nthe top of the wing and those that do strike"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71640,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it less forcefully, partly because it’s\nbeing “shielded” by its own forward motion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76070,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(the way running into the rain keeps your\nback drier) and partly because a curving stream"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80360,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of air has lower pressure on the inside of\nthe curve since the molecules get thrown centripetally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84790,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the outside."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85830,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But whatever the reasons, the pressure on\nthe top of the wing goes down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89700,
    "dDurationMs": 6710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, low pressure on the top plus high pressure\non the bottom, and the plane has lift."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96410,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if the pressure/force imbalance is big\nenough, it can lift the plane up into the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100040,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "air against gravity!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101450,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, all this crashing into air molecules\nto lift the plane also pushes to slow the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106060,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plane down – which it would, if not for\nengines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109570,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Engines also push air (in this case, backwards),\neither via a propellor, or a jet, or a jet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114680,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "driving a propellor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115680,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For various reasons, it turns out that you\nwant to have a really big propellor driven"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119310,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a really small jet for the most efficient\nengine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122240,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even in inefficient engines, the spinning\nfan blades get their horizontal lift, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126730,
    "dDurationMs": 5269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we call “thrust,” by moving quickly through\nair with a curved shape and a slightly inclined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131999,
    "dDurationMs": 2831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "angle – they’re essentially mini-wings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134830,
    "dDurationMs": 4739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so an airplane is essentially a meta-wing:\nit flies by moving mini-wings fast enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139569,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to push air molecules backwards, which moves\nthe plane forward fast enough that its big"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143790,
    "dDurationMs": 16050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wings push air molecules down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159840,
    "dDurationMs": 14590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whoa."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174430,
    "dDurationMs": 14600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wingception."
    } ]
  } ]
}
